Context for 12eeab9 (T029): MVP_SPEC.md section 8 requires that an exploration profile use an explicit starter policy, stay unvalidated, and work only in evaluation or shadow mode, so developers can try semantic checks before labels exist. The generator therefore records every starter number inside the artifact (nothing implied), refuses to invent measurements (no resolved model, translation taken offline from the adapter or the validated question), and defers all validation to the Rust core so a generated profile can never be weaker than a hand-written one. The run() gate reorder matters: enforcement must refuse an unvalidated profile before the still-pending semantic run path (T034) would mask the qualification failure. The calibrate API (T050) later replaces starter numbers with measured parameters as a new profile.
